      "Trucks-on-Trains (ToT) lets loaded trucks travel on specially modified flat wagons along a dedicated freight corridor, so the truck avoids the long highway haul and only drives the short first- and last-mile legs. Important scope note first: at present the service operates on one stretch — New Rewari to New Palanpur on the Western Dedicated Freight Corridor, roughly 636 km — not nationwide, though Indian Railways says it will extend to more sections as infrastructure develops ([PIB / Ministry of Railways, 22 January 2026](https://pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2217341&reg=3&lang=2)).",
